 the dragonglass that Sam had which  was actually Jon Snow's dagger Lord  Commander Mormont knew that every man on  the wall needed this obsidian but they  had no idea where to get it but Sam knew  that the children of the forest used  obsidian so he knew they would know  where to find it now we all know Stannis  actually told Sam that dragonglass was  on Dragonstone but Sam wasn't exactly  sure where to fire  on Dragonstone but in the book Stannis  actually told Sam exactly where it was  he told Sam that it was under the  mountain but for some reason they  changed it in the show I guess they just  did that to him could have something big  to discover while he was at the Citadel  so when we fast forward a few years  later Sam is now at the Citadel and he  finds the book that has a map of  Dragonstone that shows exactly where the  location of the dragonglass is Sam tells  Jon were to find it now Jon is on  Dragonstone hoping Daenerys will allow  him to mine for it because he too wants  to arm everyone in the north especially  the Nights Watch as we saw in the last  episode Daenerys said she would allow  Jon to mine for this dragonglass that he  so desperately wanted she even agreed to  supply him with men to help him if he  needed in the preview trailer for  episode 4 we can see Jon Snow Daenerys  and missandei walking into what looks  like a cave as Jon leads the group with  a torch now this is where the spoilers  are actually going to come into play and  some of you might not think this is a  big deal but I thought this was very  very interesting while they are down  here inside these tunnels in the cave  they're going to end up going to a  deeper and darker part of the cave and  they're actually going to discover some  cave paintings on the walls some of  these cave paintings will be the spirals  just like the spirals we have seen many  times before these paintings were  actually done by the children of the  forest and they could be very similar to  the weirwood circles that have been seen  before it's not quite the same in the  show as it is in the books  but the children have made these before  too  [Music]  Jon Snow and Daenerys realized these  cave paintings are very old and they've  been here long before the Targaryen Zoar  Starks have ever been around it says  that Daenerys thinks these paintings  date back to before there were even men  but John is going to show her another  cave painting and this one is very  interesting as well the picture John  shows her is of five small figures with  three larger one and it's the children  of the forest and the first men coming  together to fight a common enemy which  is the White Walkers then they see  another painting and there is another  group of figures but it says one of them  is clearly the night King painted on the  wall and John uses these paintings as an  example to show Daenerys that even  though they may have their differences  this proves that there has always been a  need for them to come together and fight  this enemy apparently it says that  Daenerys is going to believe John Ian  agree with him and she does agree to  help him but only if he bends the knee  now this spoiler kind of blew my mind  when I first read it the children of the  forest have always been known to live in  caves and secret tree towns and I've  always wondered where the children was  getting their obsidian from this appears  to show that the children of the forest  were actually getting their obsidian  from dragon stone - and they may have  even gotten the dragon glass they used  to create the night King from one of  these caves  [Music]  [Applause]  and I'm going to be honest with you if I  went into one of these caves and saw  cave paintings of little children of the  forest and those spirals and some White  Walkers and the night King I would be  creeped the [ __ ] out do any of you  actually think this has a deeper meaning  to it than just showing that people with  differences have had to come together  before in the past in order to defeat  their enemy  these weirwood circles and spirals keep  popping back up and are most likely  going to play some kind of a role in the  endgame we have seen these designs many  times before even back in season one  when med beheaded the man from the  Nights Watch if you look at the stone  formation around the stump the large  pieces of stone are actually in a circle  similar to how the ice blocks were in a  circular formation where the knight King  turned the baby into the white Walker  this kind of thing has always interested  me and made me very curious as to what  else this could actually mean these cave  paintings may not end up meaning much  more than what John said they proved but  they still intrigue me nonetheless and I  have a feeling we may see the children  of the forest once again I actually  don't think bran stark is going to stay  at Winterfell for the rest of his life  or at least for the rest of this series  I should say I know it seemed like the  rest of the children or the forest are  dead and they died in the cave when bran  Hodor and Meera had to escape but there  might actually be more of them at the AL  of phases where the first pact was made  brain may end up being led down there  now that he is the three-eyed Raven and  as we saw in the last episode bran  really doesn't fit in with regular  society anymore  he is so distant from everyone and has  really lost touch with most human  emotions and I feel like he's going to  need to leave Winterfell in season 8 and  if there are any more children of the  forest I think bran will have to find  them because in the books it is said  that the children of the forest can  speak with the dead they don't talk and  have language like humans do like they  did in the show so if that's the case  bran might actually have to end up being  able to do the same thing bran might  actually end up being one of the only  people who can communicate with the 19 I  think if